 "summary": "Not on their own. Pooled across BTC, ETH and SOL, all three settings did the same as random on 1h and 4h, and two of them did on daily too. Only one result beat random: the squeeze firing with positive momentum on daily. It is fragile, because a single signal on Feb 3, 2021 carries it, and it fires in volatile candles in a window that rose.",
 "verdicts": [
  {
   "use": "Squeeze fires with positive momentum",
   "verdict": "fragile",
   "text": "Same as random on 1h and 4h. On daily it beat random, but one signal on Feb 3, 2021 carries the result, and it fires in volatile candles, so it does not show price direction."
  },
  {
   "use": "Momentum crosses up zero",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random on 1h, 4h and daily."
  },
  {
   "use": "Out of a squeeze with rising momentum",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random on 1h, 4h and daily, even though it enters on every candle the condition holds."
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "On daily, price moved 6.1% more after the squeeze fired with positive momentum than after random candles, 20 candles later. The luck band topped out at 4.68%. That result comes from 100 entries, and one signal on Feb 3, 2021 carries it: leave that signal out and it falls inside the band. It also beat random at 10 candles but not at 50 or 100. On 1h and 4h the same setting landed inside the band, at 0.15% and 0.03%.",
  "The daily result comes from uptrends. When the pair closed above its 200-day SMA, the setting beat random by 6.81%, and it still did without its strongest signal on Aug 1, 2021. Below the SMA it came in at 0.62%, the same as random. The setting fires mostly in volatile candles, and the uptrend entries sit in a window where price rose. Price moved more after those candles. The setting did not pick the direction.",
  "Out of a squeeze with rising momentum enters on every candle the condition holds. On 1h its 33,312 entries form only 2,459 separate moves. Pooled, it did the same as random on 1h, 4h and daily. On daily in uptrends it beat random by 3.68%, but 39 entries between Jul 22, 2021 and Sep 10, 2021 carry that. Without them it is chance, and in downtrends it was the same as random at -1.89%. SOL on daily rests on the same stretch. This setting is volatility-timed too, so read it as price moving more in a rising window, not as a directional signal.",
  "Momentum crossing up through zero did the same as random pooled on every timeframe. On 4h in downtrends it beat random by 0.46%, but 3 entries between Aug 13, 2026 and Aug 17, 2026 carry it. In uptrends it was the same as random at -0.06%. ETH on 4h beat random by 0.67% and held without that stretch, but only at 20 candles. At 10, 50 and 100 candles it was chance.",
  "On 1h, every coin result above the band rests on a few entries. The squeeze firing on BTC depends on 2 entries on Mar 12, 2023, the USDC depeg weekend. On ETH it depends on 3 entries on Aug 18–19, 2026, and SOL's zero cross depends on 3 entries on Sep 8, 2021. Leave out each stretch and the result is chance. The BTC and ETH squeeze results also come from volatile candles, not from the setting picking direction.",
  "On a long DCA bot, none of these settings timed entries better than a random candle on 1h or 4h. You can test the squeeze firing on daily as a filter beside a trend condition, such as the pair above its 200-day SMA, where its result sat. Expect wider swings after it fires, and set the take profit and DCA step for them. In downtrends it added nothing, so leave it out of a bot that runs through both regimes."
 ],
